  "source_ref": "Terasic Agilex 7 FPGA Starter Kit User Manual v1.3.1 (2024-08-28, rev.C1 board) Table 2-21 \"FMCP Connector Pin Assignments, Signal Names and Functions\", cross-checked against Table 2-18 (clock-capable FMC+ pins). The UG lists only the positive ball of every transceiver-side pair (DP/GBTCLK/REFCLK/SYNC); negative balls derived from the Altera Agilex 7 F-Series AGFB027 device pin-out file, Pin List R24C (version 2022-09-26, Final), which also independently verifies all 122 differential pairs and confirms DP0-15 map monotonically onto F-tile FGTR13A Q0-Q3 CH0-CH3 (C2M=TX, M2C=RX). Excluded: Table 2-20 FMCP_REFCLK_p0-p3 (on-board Si5340A programmable transceiver reference clocks, not connector signals) and FMCP_RES[1] (ball CN13 - no canonical RES1 name in VITA 57.1). FMCP_RES[0] is included: it reaches the FPGA's dedicated F-tile PERST# input (CG13); the UG marks it \"For PCIe Card Applications\". GA0/GA1/SCL/SDA reach FPGA I/O through always-populated level translators (UG Table 2-21 note 2). PRSNT_M2C_L, PG_C2M, PG_M2C, CLK_DIR, VREF and the FMC+ JTAG pins are not in the UG pin table (JTAG goes to the board JTAG chain via SW3.2) and are treated as not routed to the FPGA. Terasic publishes no schematic for this board, so the data is not schematic-verified. VADJ is a fixed 1.2 V rail; the JP1 FMC_VCCIO header changes only the host-side VCCIO of the HA/HB bank (2C), not the connector VADJ.",
